# Prisma & Repository Rules

All Prisma access lives in `*.repository.ts` files only.

- Always `select` needed fields — never expose `passwordHash` or sensitive columns
- Soft delete: `where: { deletedAt: null }` on reads; set `deletedAt` instead of deleting
- Multi-table writes: `prisma.$transaction([...])`
- Catch `PrismaClientKnownRequestError`: **P2002** → Conflict, **P2025** → NotFound
- `findMany()` in production: always include `where` and/or `take`
- `vendor_transactions`: **append-only** — never update or delete

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class ProductsRepository {
  constructor(private readonly prisma: PrismaService) {}

  async findById(id: string) {
    return this.prisma.product.findFirst({
      where: { id, deletedAt: null },
      select: { id: true, name: true, slug: true, status: true },
    });
  }
}
```
